1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,470
Have you ever been alone in a room, heard someone coming, and been able to identify who it was based solely on the recognisable stomp of their shoes?
你是否曾独自在房间里，听到有人走来，仅凭他们那可识别的跺脚声就能辨认出是谁？

2
00:00:10,470 --> 00:00:21,640
Maybe you've experienced seeing a group in the distance, too far to recognise faces, but you're absolutely sure one blurry figure is your friend because of the way they're swinging their arms when they walk.
也许你经历过远远看到一群人，远到看不清脸，但你绝对确定其中一个模糊的身影是你的朋友，因为他们走路时摆动手臂的方式。

3
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:29,330
Research suggests that a person's movement signature, or the way they move, could be as unique as a fingerprint.
研究表明，一个人的动作特征，或者说他们的动作方式，可能像指纹一样独特。

4
00:00:29,330 --> 00:00:33,010
So, what makes up a person's movement signature?
那么，一个人的动作特征是由什么构成的呢？

5
00:00:33,010 --> 00:00:36,880
We all have a particular way of moving our faces.
我们都有特定的面部活动方式。

6
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:39,960
One person might purse their lips when they're angry.
一个人生气时可能会噘起嘴唇。

7
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:49,580
Another might squint their eyes or pull their face into a grimace, and these movement patterns help us recognise familiar people, even in poor visibility.
另一个人可能会眯起眼睛或做鬼脸，这些运动模式帮助我们在能见度差的情况下认出熟悉的人。

8
00:00:49,580 --> 00:00:53,810
Another reliable clue for identifying people is their gait.
另一个认人的可靠线索是他们的步态。

9
00:00:53,810 --> 00:01:01,460
The combination of stride length, limb movement, pace and posture form a movement signature that is very difficult to fake.
步幅长度、肢体运动、步速和姿势的组合形成了一种很难冒充的运动特征。

10
00:01:01,460 --> 00:01:11,590
Researchers in a 2005 study called 'Person identification from biological motion' put small lights on key parts of some male walkers' bodies.
在2005年一项名为《从生物运动中识别个体》的研究中，研究人员在一些男性行走者身体的关键部位放置了小灯。

11
00:01:11,590 --> 00:01:20,420
When the room was dark and their bodies invisible, observers were able to distinguish the walkers using the lights at an impressively high rate.
当房间黑暗且他们的身体不可见时，观察者能够通过灯光区分出行走者，成功率非常高。

12
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:24,470
Movement signatures are deeply human and expressive.
运动特征是非常人性化且富有表现力的。"

13
00:01:24,470 --> 00:01:27,310
"Dance has always been a part of my life."
舞蹈一直是我生活的一部分。"

14
00:01:27,310 --> 00:01:33,280
Brenda Loukes is a dancer and artist who uses ink and bleach to portray bodies in motion.
布伦达·卢克斯是一位舞蹈家和艺术家，她使用墨水和漂白剂来描绘运动中的身体。"

15
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:38,090
"It occurred to me that each body has a unique blueprint for the way it moves".
我突然想到，每个身体都有其独特的运动蓝图。"

16
00:01:38,090 --> 00:02:00,250
For dance writer Nancy Wozny, dancers who make it onto her list of 'ones to watch' are those who move in a way she's never seen before, like Stephanie Troyak who has a 'sublime awkwardness', reminding Nancy of a foal's 'first steps out of the womb', or how Ching Ching Wong can divide her body between 'wiggly-squiggly' and completely still.
对于舞蹈作家南希·沃兹尼来说，进入她"值得关注"名单的舞者，是以她从未见过的方式移动的人，比如斯蒂芬妮·特洛伊亚克有一种极致的笨拙感，让南希想起小马驹迈出子宫后的最初几步，或者是黄青青可以将她的身体在扭来扭去和完全静止之间自由切换。

17
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:08,700
Whether you're dancing professionally or just walking down the street, your movements reveal who you are and tell a story that no one else can replicate.
无论你是专业舞者，还是仅仅走在街上的普通人，你的动作都会揭示你是谁，并讲述一个别人无法复制的故事。
